   "t": 24.072,
   "text": "The towel is bunched inward along both sides. I\u2019m making gentle outward strokes with closed fingertips, then I\u2019ll reassess the remaining folds before grasping the corners."
  },
  {
   "t": 82.961,
   "text": "The side folds have opened substantially. I\u2019m smoothing the remaining central tuck, then I\u2019ll scoop the two near corners and lift them briefly to verify both holds."
  },
  {
   "t": 137.378,
   "text": "The towel slid toward the arms during smoothing. I\u2019m moving it back toward the center and correcting the central ripple before making the fold."
  },
  {
   "t": 169.481,
   "text": "The fingertips are just outside the two near corners. I\u2019ll check their actual positions, slide under the cloth, and verify both grips with a short lift."
  },
  {
   "t": 230.717,
   "text": "Both corners are holding, and lifting and spreading them has opened the central folds. The towel is now spread out on the table. I\u2019ll carry the held edge over in a slow arc and align it with the far edge."
  },
  {
   "t": 276.389,
   "text": "The towel is folded, but the top edge still sags inward at the center. I\u2019ll hold the lower layer steady and smooth that edge toward the opposite edge."
  },
  {
   "t": 334.061,
   "text": "The last stroke shifted one side instead of flattening the top layer. I\u2019ll correct that with a direct grip on the raised edge."
  },
  {
   "t": 399.659,
   "text": "The fold is formed, but the layers are still wrinkled. I\u2019ll lift it by the folded corners so both layers can settle, then lower it gently back onto the table."
  },
  {
   "t": 472.691,
   "text": "The towel is back on the table in a single fold. I\u2019m releasing the corners and checking the final placement."
  },
